            <ArticleTitle>Radiology Case of the Month: Persistent Lateral Foot Pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>182-183</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 33-year-old female presents with persistent lateral foot pain. Patient does not recall prior trauma that may have led to injury. Symptoms are significantly improved with rest and nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory medications.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
